\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces HOTA (\%) of SCL{} and of two simple adaptive-threshold baselines on KITTI tracking training (official HOTA, car and pedestrian averaged). Host: the tracker alone, without any layer. $t_1$, $t_2$: the adaptive baselines, in which the tracker's matching and birth thresholds are set in every frame to the first or second Otsu split of the logits of the last 10 frames, and the scores are passed unchanged. Halved: halved detector scores. $\Delta $: SCL{} minus the $t_2$ baseline, with 95\% paired-bootstrap interval below the value; bold intervals exclude zero.}}{10}{table.63}\protected@file@percent }
